 "capsule": "The Adal Sultanate, refounded at Dakkar in 1415 by Sabr ad-Din III after the Ifat Sultanate's fall, waged intermittent war on Christian Ethiopia under the Walashma dynasty and expanded under Sultan Badlay (d. 1445). Its defining era came under Imam Ahmad ibn Ibrahim al-Ghazi, whose 1529–1543 Ottoman-aided jihad conquered much of the Ethiopian highlands until his death at Wayna Daga in 1543, leaving the weakened sultanate ruled from Harar, its capital since 1520.",
